\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2.2}{\ignorespaces Two readings of a steep yield curve. Forward rates above short rates can mean that short rates will rise, as the expectations hypothesis says, or that long bonds will earn more than short ones, a term premium. The tests in this chapter measure how much of each.}}{35}{figure.caption.11}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:07-readings}{{2.2}{35}{Two readings of a steep yield curve. Forward rates above short rates can mean that short rates will rise, as the expectations hypothesis says, or that long bonds will earn more than short ones, a term premium. The tests in this chapter measure how much of each}{figure.caption.11}{}}
